[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/issues/comments/2480135614","html_url":"https://github.com/juanfont/headscale/issues/2234#issuecomment-2480135614","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/issues/2234","id":2480135614,"node_id":"IC_kwDOEFLz886T092-","user":{"login":"myOmikron","id":39948112,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM5OTQ4MTEy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/39948112?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/myOmikron","html_url":"https://github.com/myOmikron","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myOmikron/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myOmikron/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myOmikron/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myOmikron/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myOmikron/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myOmikron/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myOmikron/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myOmikron/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myOmikron/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-15T23:38:50Z","updated_at":"2024-11-15T23:38:50Z","body":"Additional information:\r\n\r\nGot it to working after installing `systemd-resolved` and linking its `stub-resolve` to `/etc/resolve.conf` like proposed in tailwinds article about Linux DNS systems on the exit-node. ","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/issues/comments/2480135614/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/issues/comments/2480465318","html_url":"https://github.com/juanfont/headscale/issues/2234#issuecomment-2480465318","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/issues/2234","id":2480465318,"node_id":"IC_kwDOEFLz886T2OWm","user":{"login":"nblock","id":131119,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzMTExOQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/131119?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nblock","html_url":"https://github.com/nblock","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nblock/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nblock/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nblock/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nblock/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nblock/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nblock/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nblock/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nblock/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nblock/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-16T07:37:18Z","updated_at":"2024-11-16T07:37:18Z","body":"> Got it to working after installing `systemd-resolved` and linking its `stub-resolve` to `/etc/resolve.conf` like proposed in tailwinds article about Linux DNS systems on the exit-node.\r\n\r\nThanks for the update, is your issue now fully resolved?\r\n\r\nFor others with DNS related issues: recent tailscale versions have a command to print the DNS status which might be helpful for debugging: `tailscale dns status`","author_association":"COLLABORATOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/issues/comments/2480465318/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/issues/comments/2482873068","html_url":"https://github.com/juanfont/headscale/issues/2234#issuecomment-2482873068","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/issues/2234","id":2482873068,"node_id":"IC_kwDOEFLz886T_aLs","user":{"login":"myOmikron","id":39948112,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM5OTQ4MTEy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/39948112?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/myOmikron","html_url":"https://github.com/myOmikron","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myOmikron/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myOmikron/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myOmikron/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myOmikron/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myOmikron/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myOmikron/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myOmikron/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myOmikron/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myOmikron/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-18T12:14:45Z","updated_at":"2024-11-18T12:14:45Z","body":"I don't think so.\r\n\r\nThe behavior I described was broken with a `resolv.conf` generated by tailscale, which pointed DNS to `100.100.100.100`. As DNS should happen on my client machine asking `100.100.100.100` directly, I think the exit-node shouldn't have anything to do with resolving.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/issues/comments/2482873068/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/issues/comments/2493778626","html_url":"https://github.com/juanfont/headscale/issues/2234#issuecomment-2493778626","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/issues/2234","id":2493778626,"node_id":"IC_kwDOEFLz886UpArC","user":{"login":"nblock","id":131119,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzMTExOQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/131119?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nblock","html_url":"https://github.com/nblock","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nblock/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nblock/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nblock/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nblock/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nblock/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nblock/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nblock/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nblock/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nblock/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-22T13:32:28Z","updated_at":"2024-11-22T13:32:28Z","body":"> I don't think so.\r\n\r\nI assume that `/etc/resolv.conf` was statically configured and tailscale overwrites the file on startup. Can you provide some logs during startup and then when you enable/disable the exit node? Given that you want to go back from `systemd-resolved` to a statically managed `/etc/resolv.conf`. DNS related configuration of your headscale might also be interesting.","author_association":"COLLABORATOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/issues/comments/2493778626/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/issues/comments/2493812033","html_url":"https://github.com/juanfont/headscale/issues/2234#issuecomment-2493812033","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/issues/2234","id":2493812033,"node_id":"IC_kwDOEFLz886UpI1B","user":{"login":"tho22","id":46346227,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ2MzQ2MjI3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/46346227?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tho22","html_url":"https://github.com/tho22","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tho22/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tho22/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tho22/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tho22/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tho22/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tho22/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tho22/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tho22/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tho22/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-22T13:48:46Z","updated_at":"2024-11-22T13:48:46Z","body":"Same problem here when --accept-dns=true\r\ninternal names are resolved. external ones are not :\r\n```\r\n$ dig nb-715.example.com @100.100.100.100 +short\r\n10.197.4.3     ###<-- same with the 100.64 Net\r\n$ dig google.com @100.100.100.100\r\n;; communications error to 100.100.100.100#53: timed out\r\n$ dig google.com @1.1.1.1 +short\r\n142.251.36.238\r\n```\r\nconfig.yaml snippet:\r\n```\r\ndns:\r\n  magic_dns: true\r\n  #  magic_dns: false\r\n  base_domain: example.com\r\n  override_local_dns: true\r\n  #override_local_dns: false\r\n  nameservers:\r\n    global:\r\n      - 1.1.1.1\r\n```\r\n\r\nstatus on the client:\r\n```\r\n$ tailscale version\r\n1.76.6\r\n  tailscale commit: 1edcf9d466ceafedd2816db1a24d5ba4b0b18a5b\r\n  other commit: d0a6cd8b27eb46f6dec31425499159f7949be7f9\r\n  go version: go1.23.1\r\n  \r\n$ tailscale dns status\r\n\r\n=== 'Use Tailscale DNS' status ===\r\n\r\nTailscale DNS: enabled.\r\n\r\nTailscale is configured to handle DNS queries on this device.\r\nRun 'tailscale set --accept-dns=false' to revert to your system default DNS resolver.\r\n\r\n=== MagicDNS configuration ===\r\n\r\nThis is the DNS configuration provided by the coordination server to this device.\r\n\r\nMagicDNS: enabled tailnet-wide (suffix = example.com)\r\n\r\nOther devices in your tailnet can reach this device at nb-715.example.com\r\n\r\nResolvers (in preference order):\r\n  - 1.1.1.1\r\n\r\nSplit DNS Routes:\r\n\r\nSearch Domains:\r\n  - example.com\r\n\r\n=== System DNS configuration ===\r\n\r\nThis is the DNS configuration that Tailscale believes your operating system is using.\r\nTailscale may use this configuration if 'Override Local DNS' is disabled in the admin console,\r\nor if no resolvers are provided by the coordination server.\r\n\r\n  (reading the system DNS configuration is not supported on this platform)\r\n\r\n[this is a preliminary version of this command; the output format may change in the future]\r\n```\r\nServer run on docker headscale/headscale:0.23.0\r\nany ideas?","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/issues/comments/2493812033/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/issues/comments/2493820540","html_url":"https://github.com/juanfont/headscale/issues/2234#issuecomment-2493820540","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/issues/2234","id":2493820540,"node_id":"IC_kwDOEFLz886UpK58","user":{"login":"nblock","id":131119,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzMTExOQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/131119?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nblock","html_url":"https://github.com/nblock","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nblock/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nblock/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nblock/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nblock/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nblock/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nblock/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nblock/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nblock/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nblock/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-22T13:52:49Z","updated_at":"2024-11-22T13:52:49Z","body":"> Same problem here when --accept-dns=true internal names are resolved. external ones are not :\r\n\r\nDo you use an exit node?","author_association":"COLLABORATOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/issues/comments/2493820540/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/issues/comments/2493911054","html_url":"https://github.com/juanfont/headscale/issues/2234#issuecomment-2493911054","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/issues/2234","id":2493911054,"node_id":"IC_kwDOEFLz886UphAO","user":{"login":"tho22","id":46346227,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ2MzQ2MjI3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/46346227?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tho22","html_url":"https://github.com/tho22","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tho22/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tho22/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tho22/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tho22/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tho22/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tho22/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tho22/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tho22/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tho22/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-22T14:38:19Z","updated_at":"2024-11-22T14:38:19Z","body":"> > Same problem here when --accept-dns=true internal names are resolved. external ones are not :\r\n> \r\n> Do you use an exit node?\r\n\r\nYes, this problem only exists with exit node constellations.\r\nFor me, I have a workaround.\r\nInstead of using \"--advertise-exit-node\", I use the routing for all \"--advertise-routes=0.0.0.0/1,128.0.0.0/1,::/1,8000::/1\".\r\n","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/issues/comments/2493911054/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/issues/comments/2525196896","html_url":"https://github.com/juanfont/headscale/issues/2234#issuecomment-2525196896","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/issues/2234","id":2525196896,"node_id":"IC_kwDOEFLz886Wg3Jg","user":{"login":"baiyz0825","id":81071870,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxMDcxODcw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81071870?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/baiyz0825","html_url":"https://github.com/baiyz0825","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/baiyz0825/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/baiyz0825/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/baiyz0825/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/baiyz0825/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/baiyz0825/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/baiyz0825/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/baiyz0825/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/baiyz0825/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/baiyz0825/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-07T14:58:31Z","updated_at":"2024-12-07T14:58:31Z","body":"i have the same problem , i check the tailscale outpot ,in my client use exit node A ,controler config the router\r\n```txt\r\nID | Node          | Prefix         | Advertised | Enabled | Primary\r\n5  | vm-0-8-ubuntu | ::/0           | true       | true    | -\r\n6  | vm-0-8-ubuntu | 0.0.0.0/0      | true       | true    | -\r\n```\r\n\r\ntailscale dns status outpput below:\r\n```txt\r\n=== 'Use Tailscale DNS' status ===\r\n\r\nTailscale DNS: enabled.\r\n\r\nTailscale is configured to handle DNS queries on this device.\r\nRun 'tailscale set --accept-dns=false' to revert to your system default DNS resolver.\r\n\r\n=== MagicDNS configuration ===\r\n\r\nThis is the DNS configuration provided by the coordination server to this device.\r\n\r\nMagicDNS: enabled tailnet-wide (suffix = headscale.vitrul)\r\n\r\nOther devices in your tailnet can reach this device at baiyz-laptop.headscale.vitrul\r\n\r\nResolvers (in preference order):\r\n  - 223.5.5.5\r\n  - 8.8.8.8\r\n  - 1.1.1.1\r\n  - 2400:3200::1\r\n  - 2001:4860:4860::8888\r\n  - 2606:4700:4700::1111\r\n  - 2606:4700:4700::1001\r\n\r\nSplit DNS Routes:\r\n\r\nSearch Domains:\r\n  - headscale.vitrul\r\n\r\n=== System DNS configuration ===\r\n\r\nThis is the DNS configuration that Tailscale believes your operating system is using.\r\nTailscale may use this configuration if 'Override Local DNS' is disabled in the admin console,\r\nor if no resolvers are provided by the coordination server.\r\n\r\nNameservers:\r\n  - 192.168.94.232\r\n\r\nSearch domains:\r\n  (no search domains found)\r\n\r\n[this is a preliminary version of this command; the output format may change in the future]\r\n```","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/issues/comments/2525196896/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/issues/comments/2656964026","html_url":"https://github.com/juanfont/headscale/issues/2234#issuecomment-2656964026","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/issues/2234","id":2656964026,"node_id":"IC_kwDOEFLz886eXg26","user":{"login":"bentemple","id":6243881,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYyNDM4ODE=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6243881?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bentemple","html_url":"https://github.com/bentemple","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bentemple/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bentemple/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bentemple/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bentemple/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bentemple/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bentemple/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bentemple/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bentemple/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bentemple/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-13T15:29:41Z","updated_at":"2025-02-13T15:39:34Z","body":"Having this same problem as well. Was trying to setup an exit-node using a tailscale docker client, but DNS resolving is broken when trying to use the exit-node.\n\nI think I got it working, I had to add the following to my exit node:\n\n     sysctls:\n       - net.ipv4.ip_forward=1\n       - net.ipv6.conf.all.forwarding=1\n \nif hosting the tailscale exit node on the host you can also add these directly to sysctls.conf\n\nThey mention this network configuration here: https://tailscale.com/kb/1408/quick-guide-exit-nodes","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/issues/comments/2656964026/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/issues/comments/2686067023","html_url":"https://github.com/juanfont/headscale/issues/2234#issuecomment-2686067023","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/issues/2234","id":2686067023,"node_id":"IC_kwDOEFLz886gGiFP","user":{"login":"kiawizard","id":7394306,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjczOTQzMDY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7394306?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kiawizard","html_url":"https://github.com/kiawizard","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kiawizard/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kiawizard/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kiawizard/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kiawizard/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kiawizard/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kiawizard/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kiawizard/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kiawizard/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kiawizard/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-26T20:01:52Z","updated_at":"2025-02-26T20:01:52Z","body":"I confirm this issue exists, Windows Exit Nodes used by Windows or Android clients do not answer to DNS queries to 100.100.100.100 for external domains while exit node is used","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/issues/comments/2686067023/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/issues/comments/2869824195","html_url":"https://github.com/juanfont/headscale/issues/2234#issuecomment-2869824195","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/issues/2234","id":2869824195,"node_id":"IC_kwDOEFLz886rDgrD","user":{"login":"clr1107","id":10479646,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwNDc5NjQ2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10479646?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/clr1107","html_url":"https://github.com/clr1107","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clr1107/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clr1107/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clr1107/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clr1107/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clr1107/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clr1107/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clr1107/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clr1107/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clr1107/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-11T12:24:30Z","updated_at":"2025-05-11T12:25:55Z","body":"Same issue here. I am not using magic dns, but have two dns resolvers set. I am using the mac tailscale client, and I am running my own dnsmasq instances to handle dns. It would be good to get this working, as I currently have to stop using an exit node to access internal resources (as they resolve via internal dns servers) and then turn it back on.\n\nIf I use `dig` it flags this warning about recursion, if that helps:\n\n```\nclr@clr-laptop ~ % dig google.com\n\n; <<>> DiG 9.10.6 <<>> google.com\n;; global options: +cmd\n;; Got answer:\n;; ->>HEADER<<- opcode: QUERY, status: SERVFAIL, id: 18615\n;; flags: qr aa rd ad; QUERY: 1, ANSWER: 0, AUTHORITY: 0, ADDITIONAL: 0\n;; WARNING: recursion requested but not available\n\n;; QUESTION SECTION:\n;google.com.\t\t\tIN\tA\n\n;; Query time: 27 msec\n;; SERVER: 100.100.100.100#53(100.100.100.100)\n;; WHEN: Sun May 11 13:22:41 BST 2025\n;; MSG SIZE  rcvd: 28\n```\n\nIf I am not using an exit node:\n\n```\nclr@clr-laptop ~ % dig google.com\n\n; <<>> DiG 9.10.6 <<>> google.com\n;; global options: +cmd\n;; Got answer:\n;; ->>HEADER<<- opcode: QUERY, status: NOERROR, id: 11453\n;; flags: qr rd ra; QUERY: 1, ANSWER: 1, AUTHORITY: 0, ADDITIONAL: 1\n\n;; OPT PSEUDOSECTION:\n; EDNS: version: 0, flags:; udp: 1232\n;; QUESTION SECTION:\n;google.com.\t\t\tIN\tA\n\n;; ANSWER SECTION:\ngoogle.com.\t\t65\tIN\tA\t216.58.201.110\n\n;; Query time: 13 msec\n;; SERVER: 100.100.100.100#53(100.100.100.100)\n;; WHEN: Sun May 11 13:22:46 BST 2025\n;; MSG SIZE  rcvd: 55\n```","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/issues/comments/2869824195/reactions","total_count":5,"+1":5,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/issues/comments/3094595139","html_url":"https://github.com/juanfont/headscale/issues/2234#issuecomment-3094595139","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/issues/2234","id":3094595139,"node_id":"IC_kwDOEFLz8864c8ZD","user":{"login":"kiawizard","id":7394306,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjczOTQzMDY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7394306?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kiawizard","html_url":"https://github.com/kiawizard","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kiawizard/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kiawizard/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kiawizard/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kiawizard/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kiawizard/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kiawizard/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kiawizard/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kiawizard/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kiawizard/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-20T15:14:25Z","updated_at":"2025-07-20T15:14:25Z","body":"Please consider raising the priority of this bug, this is critical, MagicDNS (which is on by default) does not work together with Exit Node","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/issues/comments/3094595139/reactions","total_count":9,"+1":9,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/issues/comments/3382759511","html_url":"https://github.com/juanfont/headscale/issues/2234#issuecomment-3382759511","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/issues/2234","id":3382759511,"node_id":"IC_kwDOEFLz887JoNBX","user":{"login":"djeclemen","id":6986851,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY5ODY4NTE=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6986851?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/djeclemen","html_url":"https://github.com/djeclemen","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/djeclemen/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/djeclemen/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/djeclemen/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/djeclemen/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/djeclemen/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/djeclemen/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/djeclemen/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/djeclemen/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/djeclemen/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-08T18:35:41Z","updated_at":"2025-10-08T18:35:41Z","body":"Any update?","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/issues/comments/3382759511/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/issues/comments/3397559163","html_url":"https://github.com/juanfont/headscale/issues/2234#issuecomment-3397559163","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/issues/2234","id":3397559163,"node_id":"IC_kwDOEFLz887KgqN7","user":{"login":"nblock","id":131119,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzMTExOQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/131119?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nblock","html_url":"https://github.com/nblock","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nblock/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nblock/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nblock/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nblock/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nblock/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nblock/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nblock/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nblock/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nblock/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-13T13:33:14Z","updated_at":"2025-10-13T13:33:14Z","body":"> As DNS should happen on my client machine asking 100.100.100.100 directly, I think the exit-node shouldn't have anything to do with resolving.\n\nAs stated in this [comment about DNS and exit nodes](https://github.com/tailscale/tailscale/issues/8237#issuecomment-1570581495) DNS queries are sent to the exit node and resolved on the exit node using its local DNS configuration.\n\n---\n\nFWIW, here's the gist of my working exit node setup:\n\n- No global DNS override: `dns.override_local_dns: false`\n- Exit node is Ubuntu 24.04 with systemd-resolved. It resolves all tailscale specific queries using Tailscale's DNS at 100.100.100.100 and everything else via the DNS resolver configured for the wired network interface.\n- The exit node is allowed to reach the configured DNS servers for split DNS domains: `dns.split: ...`. This might be confusing, see https://github.com/tailscale/tailscale/issues/17401\n- ACLv2 with `autogroup:internet:*` to allow some clients to use said exit node\n- Those clients are either Linux (running systemd-resolved) or Android. Both work fine and can resolve both internal and external domains\n- Headscale 0.26.1\n- Tailscale 1.88.x on all mentioned nodes","author_association":"COLLABORATOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/issues/comments/3397559163/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/issues/comments/3678627922","html_url":"https://github.com/juanfont/headscale/issues/2234#issuecomment-3678627922","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/issues/2234","id":3678627922,"node_id":"IC_kwDOEFLz887bQ2hS","user":{"login":"vborioni-onit","id":42647445,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQyNjQ3NDQ1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/42647445?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/vborioni-onit","html_url":"https://github.com/vborioni-onit","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vborioni-onit/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vborioni-onit/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vborioni-onit/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vborioni-onit/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vborioni-onit/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vborioni-onit/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vborioni-onit/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vborioni-onit/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vborioni-onit/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-12-21T09:19:23Z","updated_at":"2025-12-21T09:22:37Z","body":"Ouch, just found the issue, lost two days on this one :(\nI may add that this is the error i get with tailscail dns query, 100.64.0.1 is the ip of the exit node : \n\n\n```\nDNS query for \"www.google.com\" (A) using internal resolver:\n\nfailed to query DNS: 500 Internal Server Error: resolving using \"http://100.64.0.1:58436/dns-query\": Post \"http://100.64.0.1:58436/dns-query\": read tcp 100.64.0.2:59612->100.64.0.1:58436: wsarecv: An existing connection was forcibly closed by the remote host.\n```\n\nAnd here is the output of tailscale dns status  : \n```\n\n=== 'Use Tailscale DNS' status ===\n\nTailscale DNS: enabled.\n\nTailscale is configured to handle DNS queries on this device.\nRun 'tailscale set --accept-dns=false' to revert to your system default DNS resolver.\n\n=== MagicDNS configuration ===\n\nThis is the DNS configuration provided by the coordination server to this device.\n\nMagicDNS: enabled tailnet-wide (suffix = vpn.mydomain.it)\n\nOther devices in your tailnet can reach this device at device-1.vpn.mydomain.it.\n\nResolvers (in preference order):\n  - 1.1.1.1\n  - 8.8.8.8\n  - 1.0.0.1\n\nSplit DNS Routes:\n\nSearch Domains:\n  - vpn.mydomain.it\n\n=== System DNS configuration ===\n\nThis is the DNS configuration that Tailscale believes your operating system is using.\nTailscale may use this configuration if 'Override Local DNS' is disabled in the admin console,\nor if no resolvers are provided by the coordination server.\n\nNameservers:\n  - fde6:a348:bdb::1\n  - 2a05:9d42:407::1\n  - 192.168.10.1\n  - fde6:a348:bdb::1\n  - 2a05:9d42:407::1\n\nSearch domains:\n  (no search domains found)\n```\n","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/issues/comments/3678627922/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/issues/comments/4105129781","html_url":"https://github.com/juanfont/headscale/issues/2234#issuecomment-4105129781","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/issues/2234","id":4105129781,"node_id":"IC_kwDOEFLz8870r081","user":{"login":"github-actions[bot]","id":41898282,"node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDE4OTgyODI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/15368?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/github-actions","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/events{/priva